{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Regenerate demo Insurgency Report",
  "description": "Manual hook: rebuild a fresh local snapshot (JSON + binary) from the curated real incidents so the globe demo always has data to show.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered",
    "buttonText": "Regenerate snapshot"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Run `.venv/bin/python -m pipeline.cli --out ./frontend/public/snapshots/latest --offline --fresh --date 2026-11-14`. `--fresh` ignores the snapshot already in the folder (otherwise the CLI accumulates onto it) and the date stays pinned to 2026-11-14 so the output matches the committed fixtures. The extraction agent is mandatory, so this needs valid AWS credentials and Bedrock model access: exit code 2 means the agent preflight failed (report it and stop); exit code 3 means more than 20% of the articles were discarded, so the report was written without the new strikes (report it); exit code 4 means the existing snapshot.json is invalid and nothing was written. On success, confirm that snapshot.json and snapshot.bin were produced, report the machine-strike count and report date (strikes older than RECENCY_WINDOW_DAYS=30 relative to the report date are dropped), and verify the binary decodes by running `cd rebellion-core && cargo test decode`."
  }
}
